		{
			"date": "2012-02-20T16:04:30Z",
			"message": "sprites: fix TROO* alignment when flipped (Sodaholic)\nSodaholic writes:\n>Due to the nature of the engine's sprite flipping, the Imp was often\n>misaligned in many rotations, only way to fix it being to add\n>horizontal \"padding\" to the image. So, that's just what I did. With\n>this patch, the Imp will be correctly aligned when being viewed from\n>angles 6-8.\nDW: http://www.doomworld.com/vb/post/1052790\nSigned-off-by: RjY <rjy@users.sourceforge.net>",
			"source": "freedoom",
			"url": "https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom/commit/0181408b25fa534cae5390307dca9beba52769eb",
			"sha": "0181408b25fa534cae5390307dca9beba52769eb",
			"contributions": [
				{
					"contributorId": "nightfang",
					"relation": "Artist (from path)"
				},
				{
					"contributorId": "sodaholic",
					"relation": "Alignment fix (sprites: fix TROO* alignment when flipped)"
				},
				{
					"contributorId": "rjy",
					"relation": "Signed-off-by"
				},
				{
					"contributorId": "jonathan-dowland",
					"relation": "Committer of alignment fix"
				},
				{
					"contributorId": "archfile",
					"relation": "Committer (imp gib frames from Archfile, edited from existing TROO* and SPOS* sprites, convert PNGs to GIFs, symlink TROO[Q-U], update buildcfg.txt)"
				},
				{
					"contributorId": "julian-aubourg",
					"relation": "Implied base sprites (TROO* and SPOS*)"
				},
				{
					"contributorId": "simon-howard",
					"relation": "Committer (Import sprites)"
				}
			],
			"index": 0,
			"folder": "sprites/nightfang",
